## Architecture

I designed a single-contract, multi-escrow registry. One deployed contract holds many escrow records. Each escrow has milestones. This avoids per-escrow WASM deploy costs and keeps storage keys fine-grained, so unrelated escrows do not serialize against each other (soroban-sdk dev guide: [development.md](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stellar/stellar-dev-skill/b78983c92330d81943fa99cdaee4e4a52e85eba3/skills/smart-contracts/development.md)).

**Roles**
- `depositor` — funds the escrow, approves milestones.
- `worker` — submits milestone work.
- `arbiter` (optional) — resolves disputes.

**Data model**
- `DataKey::Admin` and `DataKey::NextId` in `instance()` storage — small, read on most calls.
- `DataKey::Escrow(u64)` in `persistent()` storage, one entry per escrow. Persistent entries survive indefinitely and can be TTL-extended; this matches the storage decision tree in the docs ([storage strategies](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/guides/storage/storage-strategies)).
- Each `Escrow` holds a `Vec<Milestone>`. Each `Milestone` holds an amount, a status, and a content hash (not raw text — keep storage small).

**Lifecycle per milestone**: `Funded → Submitted → Approved → Released`, or `Disputed → Resolved`. The depositor funds the whole escrow at creation via `token.transfer` into the contract's own balance; the contract acts as custodian and pays out per milestone on approval.

**Auth**: `depositor.require_auth()` gates create/fund/approve/cancel. `worker.require_auth()` gates submit. `arbiter.require_auth()` gates dispute resolution. The admin address is always loaded from storage, never taken as a bare parameter, per the auth guidance in [development.md](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stellar/stellar-dev-skill/b78983c92330d81943fa99cdaee4e4a52e85eba3/skills/smart-contracts/development.md#authorization).

**Token**: any SEP-41 token address, via `soroban_sdk::token::TokenClient` — this covers the Stellar Asset Contract (SAC) for USDC/XLM as well as custom tokens ([SEP-41 / token docs](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/tokens)).

## Prior art (read before reusing any code)

1. **[Trustless-Work/trustlesswork-smart-contract-stellar](https://github.com/Trustless-Work/trustlesswork-smart-contract-stellar)** — permissionless escrow infra on Soroban + USDC. Maintained, repoScore 62, code-verified against soroban-sdk 26. Symbols show `initialize_escrow`, `fund_escrow`, `release_funds`, `change_milestone_status`, `approve_milestone`, `dispute_escrow`, `resolve_dispute`, `withdraw_remaining_funds` — closest shape to what you're asking for. License/audit status unknown from this data; verify directly.
2. **[Kings9595/WaveMilestone](https://github.com/Kings9595/WaveMilestone)** — milestone pool with auto-release tied to GitHub issue closure, CI and tests present, soroban-sdk 26.1.0. Narrower use case (bounty payouts), but its `create_milestone_pool` / `release_issue_bounty` / `clawback_expired_funds` shape is a clean, small reference for the fund/release/clawback pattern.
3. **[shivamchahar99/Milestone-Payment](https://github.com/shivamchahar99/Milestone-Payment)** — closest name match to generic milestone escrow (`create_project`, `fund_milestone`, `submit_milestone`, `approve_milestone`, `dispute_milestone`, `cancel_milestone`). No CI/tests recorded and lower repoScore (14) — treat as a shape reference, not something to depend on.

These are prior art to read, not code to fork blind. None of this data confirms an audit, a license, or mainnet production use for any of the three.

## Contract skeleton

```rust
#![no_std]
use soroban_sdk::{
    contract, contracterror, contractevent, contractimpl, contracttype,
    token::TokenClient, Address, BytesN, Env, Vec,
};

// ---------- storage keys ----------

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone)]
pub enum DataKey {
    Admin,
    NextId,
    Escrow(u64),
}

// ---------- domain types ----------

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub enum MilestoneStatus {
    Funded,
    Submitted,
    Approved,
    Released,
    Disputed,
    Resolved,
}

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub struct Milestone {
    pub amount: i128,
    pub status: MilestoneStatus,
    pub description_hash: BytesN<32>,
    pub submitted_at: Option<u64>,
}

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub enum EscrowStatus {
    Active,
    Completed,
    Cancelled,
}

#[contracttype]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub struct Escrow {
    pub depositor: Address,
    pub worker: Address,
    pub arbiter: Option<Address>,
    pub token: Address,
    pub milestones: Vec<Milestone>,
    pub status: EscrowStatus,
}

// ---------- errors ----------

#[contracterror]
#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
#[repr(u32)]
pub enum Error {
    NotInitialized = 1,
    EscrowNotFound = 2,
    MilestoneNotFound = 3,
    Unauthorized = 4,
    InvalidAmount = 5,
    InvalidState = 6,
    NoMilestones = 7,
    NotActive = 8,
}

// ---------- events ----------

#[contractevent]
pub struct EscrowCreated {
    #[topic]
    pub escrow_id: u64,
    #[topic]
    pub depositor: Address,
    pub worker: Address,
    pub total: i128,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct MilestoneSubmitted {
    #[topic]
    pub escrow_id: u64,
    pub milestone_id: u32,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct MilestoneReleased {
    #[topic]
    pub escrow_id: u64,
    pub milestone_id: u32,
    pub amount: i128,
}

#[contractevent]
pub struct DisputeRaised {
    #[topic]
    pub escrow_id: u64,
    pub milestone_id: u32,
}

// ---------- TTL constants ----------

const DAY: u32 = 17_280;
const BUMP_THRESHOLD: u32 = 30 * DAY;
const BUMP_TO: u32 = 120 * DAY;

#[contract]
pub struct MilestoneEscrowContract;

#[contractimpl]
impl MilestoneEscrowContract {
    /// Runs once at deploy. Sets the platform admin (pause/upgrade authority).
    pub fn __constructor(env: Env, admin: Address) {
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::Admin, &admin);
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::NextId, &0u64);
    }

    /// Depositor creates and fully funds an escrow in one call.
    /// `amounts` sums to the total the depositor transfers into the contract.
    pub fn create_escrow(
        env: Env,
        depositor: Address,
        worker: Address,
        arbiter: Option<Address>,
        token: Address,
        amounts: Vec<i128>,
        description_hashes: Vec<BytesN<32>>,
    ) -> Result<u64, Error> {
        depositor.require_auth();

        if amounts.is_empty() || amounts.len() != description_hashes.len() {
            return Err(Error::NoMilestones);
        }

        let mut total: i128 = 0;
        let mut milestones: Vec<Milestone> = Vec::new(&env);
        for i in 0..amounts.len() {
            let amount = amounts.get(i).unwrap();
            if amount <= 0 {
                return Err(Error::InvalidAmount);
            }
            total += amount;
            milestones.push_back(Milestone {
                amount,
                status: MilestoneStatus::Funded,
                description_hash: description_hashes.get(i).unwrap(),
                submitted_at: None,
            });
        }

        // Pull the full amount into the contract's own balance up front —
        // custodial model, avoids a per-milestone funding round trip.
        let token_client = TokenClient::new(&env, &token);
        token_client.transfer(&depositor, &env.current_contract_address(), &total);

        let id: u64 = env.storage().instance().get(&DataKey::NextId).unwrap_or(0);
        env.storage().instance().set(&DataKey::NextId, &(id + 1));
        env.storage().instance().extend_ttl(BUMP_THRESHOLD, BUMP_TO);

        let escrow = Escrow {
            depositor: depositor.clone(),
            worker: worker.clone(),
            arbiter,
            token,
            milestones,
            status: EscrowStatus::Active,
        };
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Escrow(id), &escrow);
        env.storage()
            .persistent()
            .extend_ttl(&DataKey::Escrow(id), BUMP_THRESHOLD, BUMP_TO);

        EscrowCreated { escrow_id: id, depositor, worker, total }.publish(&env);
        Ok(id)
    }

    /// Worker marks a milestone as delivered.
    pub fn submit_milestone(env: Env, escrow_id: u64, milestone_id: u32) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let mut escrow = Self::load(&env, escrow_id)?;
        escrow.worker.require_auth();

        let mut m = escrow
            .milestones
            .get(milestone_id)
            .ok_or(Error::MilestoneNotFound)?;
        if m.status != MilestoneStatus::Funded {
            return Err(Error::InvalidState);
        }
        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Submitted;
        m.submitted_at = Some(env.ledger().timestamp());
        escrow.milestones.set(milestone_id, m);

        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Escrow(escrow_id), &escrow);
        MilestoneSubmitted { escrow_id, milestone_id }.publish(&env);
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Depositor approves a submitted milestone and releases its payment.
    pub fn approve_milestone(env: Env, escrow_id: u64, milestone_id: u32) -> Result<(), Error> {
        let mut escrow = Self::load(&env, escrow_id)?;
        escrow.depositor.require_auth();

        let mut m = escrow
            .milestones
            .get(milestone_id)
            .ok_or(Error::MilestoneNotFound)?;
        if m.status != MilestoneStatus::Submitted {
            return Err(Error::InvalidState);
        }

        // Effects before the external call.
        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Released;
        let amount = m.amount;
        escrow.milestones.set(milestone_id, m);
        let all_done = escrow
            .milestones
            .iter()
            .all(|x| x.status == MilestoneStatus::Released);
        if all_done {
            escrow.status = EscrowStatus::Completed;
        }
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Escrow(escrow_id), &escrow);

        let token_client = TokenClient::new(&env, &escrow.token);
        token_client.transfer(&env.current_contract_address(), &escrow.worker, &amount);

        MilestoneReleased { escrow_id, milestone_id, amount }.publish(&env);
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Either party raises a dispute on a submitted milestone; requires an arbiter.
    pub fn raise_dispute(env: Env, escrow_id: u64, milestone_id: u32, caller: Address) -> Result<(), Error> {
        caller.require_auth();
        let mut escrow = Self::load(&env, escrow_id)?;
        if caller != escrow.depositor && caller != escrow.worker {
            return Err(Error::Unauthorized);
        }
        if escrow.arbiter.is_none() {
            return Err(Error::Unauthorized);
        }

        let mut m = escrow
            .milestones
            .get(milestone_id)
            .ok_or(Error::MilestoneNotFound)?;
        if m.status != MilestoneStatus::Submitted {
            return Err(Error::InvalidState);
        }
        m.status = MilestoneStatus::Disputed;
        escrow.milestones.set(milestone_id, m);
        env.storage().persistent().set(&DataKey::Escrow(escrow_id), &escrow);

        DisputeRaised { escrow_id, milestone_id }.publish(&env);
        Ok(())
    }

    // resolve_dispute, cancel_escrow (pre-funding-consumption only),
    // and get_escrow / get_milestone read views follow the same
    // load → require_auth → check status → mutate → persist → event pattern.

    fn load(env: &Env, escrow_id: u64) -> Result<Escrow, Error> {
        let escrow: Escrow = env
            .storage()
            .persistent()
            .get(&DataKey::Escrow(escrow_id))
            .ok_or(Error::EscrowNotFound)?;
        if escrow.status != EscrowStatus::Active {
            return Err(Error::NotActive);
        }
        Ok(escrow)
    }
}
```

## Notes on this skeleton

- State updates happen before the token transfer in `approve_milestone`. Cross-contract reentrancy is blocked by the host, but ordering state before the external call is still the discipline the docs recommend.
- `submitted_at` exists so you can add a timeout-based auto-release path (a permissionless `claim_after_timeout` call, gated on `env.ledger().timestamp()`), matching the pattern in WaveMilestone's `clawback_expired_funds`.
- Every mutating call must extend the escrow's persistent-entry TTL on write. The skeleton above extends TTL only at creation — add `extend_ttl` calls to `submit_milestone` and `approve_milestone` too, or state can archive between milestone actions.
- `resolve_dispute`, `cancel_escrow`, and read-only getters are stubbed out as next steps — same load/auth/check/mutate/persist/event shape as the methods above.
- Cargo.toml: pin `soroban-sdk` to the version matching your target network protocol. Mainnet runs protocol 26 at present; use `soroban-sdk = "26"` there, not the `27.0.0-rc.1` shown for local/testnet-latest work.
- Before mainnet, work the security.md checklist referenced by the skill: authorization coverage, reinitialization guards, arithmetic overflow, storage-TTL discipline, and cross-contract call validation are the stated recurring failure modes for Soroban contracts.

Sources: [contract-anatomy / development.md](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stellar/stellar-dev-skill/b78983c92330d81943fa99cdaee4e4a52e85eba3/skills/smart-contracts/development.md), [storage strategies](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/guides/storage/storage-strategies), [TTL extension guide](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/guides/archival/test-ttl-extension), Stellar docs tokens/SEP-41 pages, and the three GitHub repos linked above.

